\description{
Instead of drawing a continuous stroke, these geoms render a regular grid of
dots and display only those within \code{radius} of the path. At fine \code{dot_spacing}
the result closely resembles \code{\link[ggplot2:geom_path]{ggplot2::geom_path()}} / \code{\link[ggplot2:geom_line]{ggplot2::geom_line()}}
/ \code{\link[ggplot2:geom_step]{ggplot2::geom_step()}}; as \code{dot_spacing} increases the discrete, stippled
character becomes visible. Dot density is constant in physical units -- the
grid reflows automatically when the viewer is resized.

\code{geom_stipple_line()} orders observations along the independent axis before
connecting them (like \code{\link[ggplot2:geom_line]{ggplot2::geom_line()}}).

\code{geom_stipple_step()} approximates a stair-step path (like
\code{\link[ggplot2:geom_step]{ggplot2::geom_step()}}); \code{direction} controls the step shape.
}
\details{
